WHEREAS, the Town of Pine Mountain offers its retirees with 10 or more years of service Georgia Municipal Employees Benefit System (GMEBS) Retiree-Only Health Plan coverage and subsidizes the cost of such coverage;

WHEREAS, effective July 31, 2017, the Georgia Municipal Association (GMA) will no longer offer this retiree-only plan coverage for retirees and spouses enrolled in the plan who are age 65 and older;

WHEREAS, in connection with this termination of coverage, the GMA is offering replacement coverage through OneExchange, a Willis Towers Watson private exchange that offers individual Medicare Supplemental Insurance (Medigap), Medicare Advantage, and Medicare Part D Prescription Drug Plans (“Medicare Plans”);

WHEREAS, the Town of Pine Mountain would like to continue to subsidize the cost of such retiree coverage by adopting a health reimbursement arrangement (HRA) through Swerdlin & Company, which will allow retirees to be reimbursed for the new Medicare Plans coverage offered through OneExchange;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, that, due to the termination by GMA of the GMEBS Retiree-Only Health Plan for retirees age 65 and older, effective July 31, 2017, the Town of Pine Mountain hereby adopts the private exchange of OneExchange, and the HRA of Swerdlin & Company to allow the Town to subsidize the cost of Medicare Plans coverage for those retirees and spouses age 65 and older who qualify for retiree coverage with 10 or more years of service with the Town;

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that the Town of Pine Mountain shal! annually determine the amount to be contributed to the HRA to allow for the reimbursement of coverage under the

